        "original_id": "0f11c43c-4eba-54cc-bfff-af8fe77bef6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Samuel Johnson\n- Organizations: Manchester United F.C., Newton Heath LYR Football Club, Tonge\n- Places: Manchester, Old Trafford\n- Topics: club founding, name changes, player career moves\n\nFacts:\n- Manchester United F.C. was founded as Newton Heath LYR Football Club in 1878.\n- Samuel Johnson was born in Manchester and began his career with Tonge.\n- Samuel Johnson moved to Newton Heath in January 1901.\n- Newton Heath LYR Football Club changed its name to Manchester United in 1902.\n- Manchester United F.C. is nicknamed \"the Red Devils.\"\n- Manchester United F.C. moved to its current stadium, Old Trafford, in 1910.",
